WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.875
Operators report consistent successful cluster deployments

00:00:03.883 --> 00:00:07.629
with pipeline post-configuration and successful cluster recoveries

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.426
using ZTF Orchestrator.

00:00:09.841 --> 00:00:14.099
Recovering Cluster A begins with a trusted Orchestrator, approved images

00:00:14.278 --> 00:00:16.169
and reviewed configuration.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:19.770
This is a simulated walkthrough, not an actual rebuild.

00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:24.288
Add or select the recovery datacenter, review prerequisites, and link

00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:28.961
one Foundation VM YAML with the intended post-configuration pipeline.

00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:33.825
Create the recovery profile and inspect its revision, exact nodes, image

00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:37.132
selections, credentials and ordered pipeline.

00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:40.174
Mark the baseline reviewed through the existing controls.

00:00:40.345 --> 00:00:42.726
An edited profile creates a new draft;

00:00:42.777 --> 00:00:45.734
an existing run keeps its original snapshot.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.984
No physical deployment happens while preparing these records.

00:00:49.262 --> 00:00:50.692
Choose Recover Cluster.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.030
If an open run exists, select Resume Recovery and inspect its current

00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:59.724
stage. For a new run, review targets and readiness, prepare recovery

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.750
and obtain the deployment approval.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.534
Confirm the destructive scope before imaging.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.922
Submit once and monitor the existing Foundation job.

00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:12.587
After imaging, complete the approved initial-access bootstrap and verify

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.946
the replacement account.

00:01:14.161 --> 00:01:18.462
Provide the required fresh PE identity, membership and health evidence before

00:01:18.641 --> 00:01:20.020
remaining configuration.

00:01:20.262 --> 00:01:24.593
Resolve collection errors or use the documented independent evidence procedure.

00:01:24.715 --> 00:01:28.192
A certificate failure must not silently become a healthy result.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.601
In this example, steps zero one through zero seven succeed

00:01:32.651 --> 00:01:35.097
and only PC registration fails.

00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:39.243
Reconcile PE and PC and confirm registration is absent.

00:01:39.407 --> 00:01:43.623
Record fresh health evidence, then use the eligible step zero eight-only

00:01:43.674 --> 00:01:48.060
retry. Show one new registration submission, unchanged earlier

00:01:48.111 --> 00:01:49.788
jobs and no new imaging.

00:01:50.136 --> 00:01:54.352
Review completed configuration, infrastructure health and the recorded acceptance

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.840
evidence. Hand workload restoration to your backup platform and verify it

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.891
separately. Preserve run history and approvals;

00:02:02.027 --> 00:02:05.646
do not treat the simulated success shown here as a production recovery

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:06.922
certification.
